I step out of the building.
I walk towards the bus stop.
The bus stop is near my home.
Some people are standing there.
In a short while, a red BEST bus arrives.
I board the bus through the back door.
Today, there are many people in the bus.
I hold the bus handrail securely.
The conductor comes near me.
I say, 'Brother, one ticket.'
I give him fifteen rupees.
He gives me a ticket.
I put the ticket in my bag.
The bus moves forward quickly.
I look outside through the window.
Mumbai's roads are very busy.
People are going to their work.
I like this morning commute.
